{
  "header": {
    "description": "The National Library of Israel's file id (FL id) of each of images 1-495 of volume 2 of its record NNL_ALEPH990000991240205171 for St. Petersburg, National Library of Russia, Evr. II B 55, the volume that the folders of Ben's download call Part B. The download holds volume 2's images 1-4 and 496-989, and their filenames carry their ids. de_nli_image is an image's canvas number in volume 2, which the NLI's viewer labels Page n, and de_fl_id is its file id. The viewer's link to an image is https://www.nli.org.il/en/manuscripts/NNL_ALEPH990000991240205171/NLI?volumeItem=2#$ followed by its de_fl_id; open it in a fresh tab, because a change to the part after # alone does not move the viewer. Images 1-363 have FL = 48717893 + de_nli_image; from image 364 the ids rise irregularly. A Claude session (Claude Code, Opus 5.5) read every id from the viewer's image list, whose manifest is https://iiif.nli.org.il/IIIFv21/DOCID/NNL_ALEPH21185775100005171/manifest/IE48716902, through Claude in Chrome on 2026-09-26. It checked them the same day: the ids rise strictly across all 989 canvases of volume 2; images 1-363 follow the formula; images 364-409 equal the ids that an earlier Claude session's analysis of the manifest gave on 2026-09-25; and the viewer's ids for images 1-4 and 496-989 give the same two sums, of the ids and of each id times its image number, as the ids in the download's 498 filenames. The file holds no text and no reading. See README.md, section Reaching images 005-495 online."
  },
